{"name":"Last Straw","hex":"#e3dbcd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"last straw","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small addition to an already heavy burden which causes it to exceed the capacity."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/last_straw"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Last Straw (1920 film)","blocks":[{"text":"The Last Straw is a lost 1920 American silent Western film directed by Denison Clift and Charles Swickard and starring Buck Jones, Vivian Rich, and Jane Talent. It cost $31,000 to make, considerably exceeding its planned budget. It was Jones' first starring role."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/The_Last_Straw_%281920%29_-_1.jpg/330px-The_Last_Straw_%281920%29_-_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Last_Straw_(1920_film)","wikidata":"Q21869512"},{"title":"The Last Straw (1987 film)","blocks":[{"text":"The Last Straw is a Canadian comedy film, released in 1987. Directed by Giles Walker and written by Walker and David Wilson, the film is a sequel to the films The Masculine Mystique and 90 Days."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Last_Straw_(1987_film)","wikidata":"Q28840540"},{"title":"Last Straw","blocks":[{"text":"Last Straw is a 2023 American horror-thriller film directed by Alan Scott Neal, written by Taylor Sardoni, and produced by Dane Eckerle, Daniel Brandt, Phil Keefe and Cole Eckerle. Starring Jessica Belkin, Taylor Kowalski, and Jeremy Sisto, the film focuses on a young waitress who fights for her life over the course of one long night when a small town killing spree lands on the doorstep of a rural diner."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Last_Straw","wikidata":"Q131154650"},{"title":"Last","blocks":[{"text":"A last is a mechanical form used by shoemakers and cordwainers in the manufacture and repair of shoes. Lasts come in many styles and sizes, depending on the exact job they are designed for. Common variations include simple one-size lasts used for repairing soles and heels, custom-purpose mechanized lasts used in modern mass production, and custom-made lasts used in the making of bespoke footwear. Lasts are made of firm materials—hardwoods, cast iron, and high-density plastics—to withstand contact with wetted leather and the strong forces involved in reshaping it. Since the early 19th century, lasts typically come in pairs to match the separate shapes of the right and left feet. The development of an automated lasting machine by the Surinamese-American Jan Ernst Matzeliger in the 1880s was a major development in shoe production, immediately improving quality, halving prices, and eliminating the previous putting-out systems surrounding shoemaking centers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/PikiWiki_Israel_13497_shoe_trees.JPG/330px-PikiWiki_Israel_13497_shoe_trees.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Last","wikidata":"Q1069931"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Schuhmacherwerkstatt_HH.jpg/500px-Schuhmacherwerkstatt_HH.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Schuhmacherwerkstatt_HH.jpg/500px-Schuhmacherwerkstatt_HH.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wooden lasts in a shoemaker's workshop in Hamburg, Germany","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASchuhmacherwerkstatt_HH.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Jan_ernst_matzeliger.gif/500px-Jan_ernst_matzeliger.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Jan_ernst_matzeliger.gif/500px-Jan_ernst_matzeliger.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Jan Ernst Matzeliger in 1885","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJan_ernst_matzeliger.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Zwikmachine_1885.jpg/250px-Zwikmachine_1885.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4f/Zwikmachine_1885.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Zwikmachine_1885.jpg/250px-Zwikmachine_1885.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Matzeliger's lasting machine, complex enough the patent office had to send an agent to Lynn to see it in operation","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZwikmachine_1885.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Museo_Ferragamo_-_forme.jpg/500px-Museo_Ferragamo_-_forme.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Museo_Ferragamo_-_forme.jpg/1280px-Museo_Ferragamo_-_forme.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Museo_Ferragamo_-_forme.jpg/500px-Museo_Ferragamo_-_forme.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The personal lasts of Audrey Hepburn and Ava Gardner at the Ferragamo Museum in Florence, Italy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMuseo_Ferragamo_-_forme.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Shoemakers_tripartite_metal_last_pre_1950s_Gothenburg_Sweden.jpg/330px-Shoemakers_tripartite_metal_last_pre_1950s_Gothenburg_Sweden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Shoemakers_tripartite_metal_last_pre_1950s_Gothenburg_Sweden.jpg/960px-Shoemakers_tripartite_metal_last_pre_1950s_Gothenburg_Sweden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Shoemakers_tripartite_metal_last_pre_1950s_Gothenburg_Sweden.jpg/330px-Shoemakers_tripartite_metal_last_pre_1950s_Gothenburg_Sweden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShoemakers_tripartite_metal_last_pre_1950s_Gothenburg_Sweden.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Shoemakers_metal_last_on_stand_pre_1950s_Gothenburg_Sweden.jpg/250px-Shoemakers_metal_last_on_stand_pre_1950s_Gothenburg_Sweden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Shoemakers_metal_last_on_stand_pre_1950s_Gothenburg_Sweden.jpg/500px-Shoemakers_metal_last_on_stand_pre_1950s_Gothenburg_Sweden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Shoemakers_metal_last_on_stand_pre_1950s_Gothenburg_Sweden.jpg/250px-Shoemakers_metal_last_on_stand_pre_1950s_Gothenburg_Sweden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShoemakers_metal_last_on_stand_pre_1950s_Gothenburg_Sweden.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Wooden_lasts2.jpg/500px-Wooden_lasts2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Wooden_lasts2.jpg/960px-Wooden_lasts2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Wooden_lasts2.jpg/500px-Wooden_lasts2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaig